<Project>
  <!-- ==========================================================================
       SBPR.QaHarness.T022 — QA-only test-helper (ADR-0009 M0 skeleton)
       ==========================================================================
       UNLIKE tests/ and qa-operator-harness/ (whose local Directory.Build.props
       deliberately do NOT import the repo root, shielding their engine-free
       subtrees from the Valheim/BepInEx SDK gate), THIS helper is a BepInEx
       plugin: it must reference the Valheim managed assemblies + BepInEx core to
       touch the game. So it IMPORTS the repo-root props to inherit the proven
       $(ValheimManaged) / $(BepInExCore) resolution (env var / .env fallback) and
       the SbprValidateSdkPaths early-failure guard — the same gate the product
       assemblies use.

       ADR-0009 §1 (Location, identifiers, references, dependency boundary):
         "Helper build: net48; own Directory.Build.props that imports the repo-root
          props (it needs $(ValheimManaged)/$(BepInExCore)) but sets its own
          AssemblyName, GUID, <TreatWarningsAsErrors>true."

       The M0 skeleton is INERT: the plugin only logs a DISARMED banner and returns
       (no verbs, hooks, sockets, RPCs, files, timers, or mutation). The channels,
       gate, fixtures, actions, and runner arrive in later milestones (M1–M5) —
       each its own reviewed card.
       ========================================================================== -->
  <Import Project="$([MSBuild]::GetPathOfFileAbove('Directory.Build.props', '$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)../'))" />
</Project>
